Z||000001||theogre||11-21-2000||07:45 PM||||I know the Fiero V6 was also used in Cavalier Z24s. I think some 6000s got it to. If it looks like the Fiero motor it likely is. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||11-21-2000||10:25 PM||||It is technically the same block, but is not the exact same engine as a whole.  It had a seperate engine code and is rated at less power than the Fiero engine.  I don't know if the difference is merely intake/exhaust or more in depth from the heads to the cams and pistons.  I am thinking tis internal stuff.  You can certainly get more power by upgrading to a L44 2.8 (Fiero engine) or step up to a newer 3.1L or 3.4! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||11-21-2000||10:37 PM||||My son actually has an 85SE with the Pontiac 6000 2.8L engine in it.  If they had done the swap correctly they would have swapped the Fiero V6 intake onto it instead of leaving the 6000 stock plenum (facing the wrong way). This thing barely runs.   I don't believe it has anything to do with the engine, but I am sure they have not hooked up the engine electronics properly.  I am dropping the whole cradle and replacing it with a 2.8 auto that I am getting from someone.<BR>||||reg||1
